/*
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Component gate resource cap for this development host
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Personal-track development infrastructure. It is not part of the portable pipeline
    and never enters an upstream pipeline or component diff.

    `nf-core/modules` sets `process { cpus = 4; memory = '15.GB'; time = '2.h' }` in
    `tests/config/nf-test.config`. This machine has 13 GB of RAM in total, so a component
    gate run in an `nf-core/modules` worktree asks the local executor for more memory than
    the host owns and the run is refused before any task starts.

    `nf-test -c` takes an nf-test config, not a Nextflow config, so this file cannot be
    handed to `nf-test` directly: it is rejected as an nf-test config syntax error. It
    reaches Nextflow through `host_test_config.config` beside it, which keeps the
    repository's own `tests/config/nf-test.config` and adds this cap after it, and which
    `host_nf-test.config` names as its `configFile`. The invocation is in step 6 of
    `SKILL.md`.

    It is a ceiling, not a declaration: a component whose own test asks for less keeps
    what it asked for, and the cap changes no component's committed resource label. Drop
    the whole chain on a host that has the 15 GB the upstream default assumes.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/

process {
    resourceLimits = [
        cpus: 4,
        memory: 8.GB,
        time: 2.h,
    ]
}
